Algorithm
1. Create a weighted graph of the courier hub and service areas.
2. For shortest distances, ask the user for a source vertex; set its distance to zero and all others to infinity.
3. Run Dijkstra’s algorithm using a min-priority queue. Relax each edge when a shorter route is found.
4. For a complete path, store each vertex’s parent when its distance improves; trace parents from destination to
source and reverse the sequence.
5. For an edge update, validate the endpoints and new non-negative weight, then update both directions of the
bidirectional road.
6. Run Dijkstra’s algorithm again after the update and display the recalculated distances.
7. Report vertices whose distances remain infinite as unreachable.
Note: Dijkstra’s algorithm requires non-negative road distances.
